
Use cases on Notebook utility in real project

✅ 1. ETL Pipeline Orchestration (Most Common)
📌 Scenario

You have:

Notebook 1 → Ingest (Bronze)
Notebook 2 → Transform (Silver)
Notebook 3 → Aggregate (Gold)

🔥 Main Notebook (Controller)
dbutils.notebook.run("bronze_ingestion", 300)

👉 Runs step by step pipeline

📤 Child Notebook (example: bronze)
dbutils.notebook.exit("Bronze Completed")

📥 Capture result
result = dbutils.notebook.run("bronze_ingestion", 300)
print(result)




✅ 2. Dynamic Pipeline (Parameter Passing)
📌 Scenario

Same notebook processes different tables

🔥 Parent Notebook
tables = ["customers", "orders"]

for t in tables:
    dbutils.notebook.run("process_table", 300, {"table_name": t})

📤 Child Notebook
table = dbutils.widgets.get("table_name")

print(f"Processing {table}")

dbutils.notebook.exit(f"{table} done")


✅ 3. Error Handling & Retry Logic
📌 Scenario

If child notebook fails → retry

try:
    dbutils.notebook.run("critical_job", 60)
except Exception as e:
    print("Retrying...")
    dbutils.notebook.run("critical_job", 60)



✅ 4. Conditional Execution (Real Business Logic)
📌 Scenario

Run next step only if previous succeeds

result = dbutils.notebook.run("data_validation", 120)

if result == "success":
    dbutils.notebook.run("load_gold", 300)
else:
    print("Validation failed")


⚠️ Important Points
❗ Timeout matters
dbutils.notebook.run("sample", 60)

👉 If notebook runs > 60 sec → FAIL ❌

❗ Return only STRING
dbutils.notebook.exit("success")

❗ Use widgets for parameters
dbutils.widgets.text("param", "")



🔥 Real Project Summary
Main Notebook
   ↓
Call Bronze → exit("success")
   ↓
Call Silver → exit("success")
   ↓
Call Gold
